      "id": 495660,
      "username": "Smit_Vora",
      "name": "Smit Vora",
      "created_at": "2026-03-09T09:54:41.841Z",
      "cooked": "<p>The way this is designed in Bill of entry is all taxes are divided into two components:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Credit not available (Total Customs Duty)</li>\n<li>Credit available (IGST)</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Assessable value is editable if customs choose to have one different from your books.<br>\nSWS, BCD etc should all be added to total total customs duty. There is no added benefit of accounting it separately AFAIK.</p>",
